# 00_Cerebrum vault — tracked: Wiki bundles, Raw, Outputs, docs, scripts.
# Untracked, by decision of 09.08.2026:

# The archive layers. Read-only bulk exports, 3.8 GB, they never change and
# do not belong in a git history. This matches "a repo over the vault with
# OneNote/ ignored".
OneNote/

# The Raw layers, excluded on the owner's instruction of 10.08.2026, analog
# to OneNote: git holds the distilled knowledge, the filesystem holds the sources.
# The registry stays tracked so the repo still records what Raw holds even
# though it no longer holds it.
**/Raw/*
!**/Raw/_INGESTED.md

# Owner testimony, moved to the vault root by the three-way split of
# 15.08.2026. Same class as Raw: source material, not distilled knowledge.
# It sits here rather than in a knowledge base because each transcript covers
# all three employers and is cited from all three bundles.
_testimony/

# Retirement bins. Files here await manual deletion (the session VM cannot
# delete); they are not knowledge and must not reach GitHub. Git history is
# the real archive of retired concepts once this repo exists.
_to_delete/

# App state, not knowledge.
.obsidian/
.cogito-folder.json
.DS_Store

# Python bytecode. Generated by _scripts/ on every run; the .py files are the
# record, the .pyc files are noise that churns on every Python version bump.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Derived output of _scripts/visualize.py; regenerate rather than track.
00_Cerebrum_viewer.html
00_Cerebrum_viewer.html.tmp
# Its name until 14.09.2026. Still ignored, so a stray copy made by an old
# script or restored by a sync client is never committed as a 15 MB file.
okf-viewer.html

# Derived cache of _scripts/namescan.py; regenerate rather than track.
_scripts/.namescan-cache.json

# Packed batches and inventories: derived working files of a compile run,
# regenerated by _scripts/prepare-batch.py. The extraction files themselves
# ARE tracked — they are what an agent handed back and what merge-appends.py
# replays — but the packs are just the archive re-arranged.
**/_extractions/_packed-*.txt
**/_extractions/_INVENTORY.md
**/_extractions/raw-text/
**/.coverage-state.json

# FUSE leftovers: created when a file is renamed while still open.
# One reached a commit on 15.08.2026 from merge-appends.py archiving a handback.
.fuse_hidden*

# Archive snapshots. Fingerprint and inventory files carry per-page data
derived from the gitignored archive layers, so tracking them reopened the
boundary OneNote/ is excluded for. Found 22.08.2026, when a fingerprint's
preview column was found carrying a certificate passphrase in clear.
_snapshots/

# Claude Code project state. `.claude/skills/` is tracked — it is how a local
# session reaches the three skills — but everything the harness writes for
# itself is machine-local and must not travel.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills
.claude/settings.local.json

# The harness's own search index over the vault: a SQLite database and its
# write-ahead log, 185 MB on 06.09.2026 and rewritten whenever the corpus
# changes. Same class as `.claude/*` — machine-local, regenerable, and no part
# of the knowledge. It sat untracked and unignored from 03.09.2026, which is
# one `sh _scripts/sync.sh` away from a 185 MB binary in the history: that
# script stages with `git add -A` and would not have asked.
.context/

# Node dependencies for _scripts/viewer-check.js. The lockfile and manifest are
# tracked so the viewer check's dependency is recorded — playwright was missing
# on 31.08.2026 and nothing said it was needed; node_modules/ is not.
node_modules/

# The emailable build of the loop page. Derived, and unlike the PNGs beside it
# genuinely reproducible: `python3 _scripts/loop-page.py --standalone` rebuilds
# it byte-identically, proven 02.09.2026. It also carries 75 KB of base64 woff2,
# which repo_hygiene() reads as a credential-shaped token — the same false
# positive it already documents for a PDF's compressed streams, and one more
# reason this belongs beside the vault rather than in git.
Outputs/_figures/**/00_Cerebrum-read-repair-remember.html
